{
    "background_story": "Zayne was a brilliant linguist who spent his career studying the intricacies of language. He was particularly fascinated by descriptivism, the approach to language that focuses on describing how people actually use words and grammar, rather than prescribing how they should be used. Zayne's research took him to remote corners of the world, where he immersed himself in local dialects and cultures. He was known for his meticulous fieldwork, spending hours recording and transcribing conversations to identify patterns and trends. Zayne's work challenged traditional notions of language and grammar, revealing the complex and dynamic nature of human communication. His groundbreaking research earned him international recognition, and he became a leading voice in the field of linguistics, inspiring a new generation of scholars to explore the complexities of language.",
